module DASHI.Physics.YangMills.BalabanYM4GramWedgeIdentityGeneralExact where

------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- EXACT GRAM / WEDGE ALGEBRA IN ARBITRARY FINITE DIMENSION
--
-- WHY THIS MODULE EXISTS.  `BalabanYM4GramWedgeIdentityExact` established the
-- parallel/transverse (Gram) architecture on an explicit THREE-dimensional
-- rational carrier.  That was enough to fix the shape of the argument, but it
-- is the wrong carrier for Yang-Mills: the constrained-Gaussian fluctuation
-- space of Row A1b, the marked-source coordinate space of Row B and the
-- tangent space of Row C are all high dimensional, and a reader is entitled to
-- object that a three-dimensional identity is a toy.
--
-- This module removes that objection.  Every statement of the three-
-- dimensional core is reproved on `Vec ℚ n` for an ARBITRARY n, with no
-- dimension-dependent step:
--
--   * `lagrangeIdentity`     G(a,b) = sum over all index pairs i<j of the
--                            squared 2x2 minors (a_i b_j - a_j b_i)^2.
--                            Proved by induction on the dimension, via the
--                            exact expansion `crossSumExpand`.
--   * `gramNonNeg`           Cauchy-Schwarz in Q^n, exactly, as a corollary.
--   * `gramLowerBoundMinor`  EVERY single squared minor is a lower bound for
--                            the Gram determinant -- for arbitrary distinct
--                            indices i, j, not merely for the first two
--                            coordinates.  This is the general form of the
--                            non-collinearity certificate.
--   * `projectionIdentity`   |s b - t a|^2 = s * G(a,b) with s = |a|^2,
--                            t = <a,b>: the transverse residual and the Gram
--                            surplus are the same number up to |a|^2.
--   * `residualOrthogonal`   the residual is exactly orthogonal to a.
--   * `gramDichotomy`        the quantitative alternative: either the
--                            transverse residual is coercive with constant
--                            |a|^2 * delta, or the pair is delta-nearly
--                            collinear.
--
-- The projection identity is *not* proved componentwise here: it is derived
-- from genuine bilinearity of the inner product (`dot-scaleˡ`, `dot-subˡ`,
-- `dot-comm`), so the argument is the coordinate-free one and would transfer
-- verbatim to any inner-product space.
--
-- `dot-ofVec3` / `gram-ofVec3` pin the general carrier to the existing
-- three-dimensional one, so the Row A1b, Row C and A<->B consumers built on
-- `BalabanYM4GramWedgeIdentityExact` are instances of the general theory
-- rather than a separate development.
--
-- WHAT THIS IS NOT.  Nothing here is a Yang-Mills theorem, and nothing here
-- closes a row.  It is the shared exact-arithmetic core, now in the right
-- generality.  The frozen research count (4) is untouched: what the physical
-- rows still need is an identification of the literal Yang-Mills second
-- variation / marked functional / Hessian with objects of this shape, and
-- that identification is exactly what remains open.
--
-- Exact rational arithmetic; no postulate, no hole, no receipt.  Checked with
-- `agda --safe`.
------------------------------------------------------------------------

